[157.438719, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[157.482279, "o", "A measurement = a hash of exactly what is loaded. A TEE reports its measurements in a signed\r\nattestation; a key service releases a key only if they match the values you reviewed.\r\nLab stand-in: SHA-256 of each file in a model folder, then one hash over those hashes.\r\n\r\n"]
[157.482521, "o", "models/approved-model\r\n  config.json         2b9fb1f5e18062089a04138d...\r\n  model.safetensors   8a9e4d73c5036faa851d60b5...\r\n  measurement         932d715fe8fcdb87863a5027...\r\n  reviewed value      932d715fe8fcdb87863a5027...   (pinned in explore.py)\r\n  -> MATCH: the key would be released\r\n\r\n"]
[157.482621, "o", "the same folder with ONE bit of model.safetensors flipped (in memory only; the file is unchanged)\r\n  measurement         8caf645a6862c7476d979c3e...   -> NO MATCH: the key stays locked\r\n"]
[157.482779, "o", "models/suspicious-model (other files, other code)\r\n  measurement         2d8c37e2d2fac6836a09f816...   -> NO MATCH: the key stays locked\r\n\r\nA match proves WHICH files are loaded. It does not prove they are safe: that is what your review is for.\r\n"]
[157.489027, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m26\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m26\u001b[00m$ "]
